From b9ee1144f88424122612c049515f4d34b8949b62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:12:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: game data from an ISO 9660 disc image, SYSTEM.CNF
 boot, settings file

The runner took the boot ELF of an extracted folder and served cdrom0:
from that folder with pseudo LSNs. It now also takes a disc image or the
folder itself:

- ps2x/iop/iso9660.h (ps2xIOP): read-only ISO 9660 image. Primary volume
  descriptor at sector 16, path lookup (case-insensitive, '\' or '/',
  optional device prefix and ";N" on either side, unsorted records,
  zero padding at sector ends), sector and byte reads through one host
  handle per image under a mutex, no seek when a read continues the last
  one, 64 KiB stdio buffer; never loads the image. One shared instance
  per path (IsoImage::shared) for the EE, the VFS and the IOP.
- EE sceCdSearchFile/sceCdRead (Stubs/Helpers/Support.h): with an ISO
  image mounted, the file's real LSN and size from the image directory,
  sectors read from the image (was: reopened per read with ifstream,
  only reached for LBNs outside the pseudo map).
- VFS: PS2VfsMounts::cdImage; cdrom0: open/read/seek/stat inside the
  image (read only), no host path for it.
- IOP: cdvdman sceCdSearchFile/sceCdRead use the image; module loads
  from cdrom0: open image-backed host handles (PS2IopHostAdapter).
- Boot (main.cpp, runtime/ps2_game_source.h): the game is an ISO image
  (boot ELF = SYSTEM.CNF BOOT2 read from the image,
  PS2Runtime::loadELFImage; mc0 and host: beside the image), an
  extracted folder (BOOT2 of its SYSTEM.CNF) or the boot ELF (as
  before). The command line wins; else the settings file's game; on
  Android the one .iso in the app's external files dir.
- Settings file: PS2X_SETTINGS or <exe dir>/outbreak.ini (Android: the
  external files dir), read once: game, textures (PCSX2 layout
  <root>/<serial>/replacements, recorded and logged only), mods
  (reserved). Bad lines logged once as [settings] line N.

Tests (ps2x GameSource, 8 cases, synthetic 27-sector image built in the
test): lookup rules, sector reads, sequential reads seek once, BOOT2 and
serial, image and folder sources, sceCdSearchFile real LSN + sceCdRead,
cdrom0: file I/O in the image, settings parsing. With the EE/VFS
changes reverted the image cases fail (512/514).
